Now! Let's define the main loop in natural words.

The default defination of this mainloop, we copy/paste the general idea of the Internet


// One Frame means one whole main loop is done.
//
void mainloop_V1(void)
{
    // Caution! Render() means, QT GUI painting!
    // So, maybe should reduce the calculation

    calculate time of each frame time?

    do Object Property update

    do QT GUI Paint
}


void mainloop_V2_From_Unity(void)
{
    // Just simply copy/paste event loop from Unity, at first.

    Awake
      |
    OnEnable
      |
    Reset
      |
    Start
      |
    FixedUpdate -- Internal animation update -- Internal physics update -- Internal animation update
      |
    Input Events
      |
    Update  --  Game Logic
      |
    Scene Rendering (Unclear here, the difference from FixedUpdate)
      |
    GUI Rendering
      |
    End of frame
      |
    Application Pause
      |
    Application Quit

}

########################################################################################################

The Golden Rule:
    
    1. The Game, the core of it, is the Calculation.
    2. All objects are only having States and Status. States and Status can be changedable or not.
    3. User inputs, and the World Rules (Designed), CAN change objects States and Status.
    4. First, The Game, this whole world is working as the Golded Rule ---- All Objects, are changing and being changed, by "User Inputs" and "Pre-designed Rules", ONLY.
    5. Second, each "Minimum Operation" can ONLY happen in a Line, which means all things have to happen/be happened, one by one, step by step. So the order/sequence of these happening, is most important, in the Calculation.
